        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dc χT at 300 K is 49.40 cm3 K mol−1 (predicted 51.03). On cooling, χT decreases then rises (AF Cr–Ln with ferrimagnetic arrangement); χTmax 66.04 cm3 K mol−1 at 2.8 K, χTmin 40.79 at 14.0 K, χT(2 K) 64.39. M(7 T, 2 K) = 21.35 μB. Frequency-dependent ac χ′ and χ″ in zero dc field show SMM slow relaxation; Arrhenius fit of 1.8–2.3 K data gives Δ = 24.1 K and τ0 = 4.0×10−9 s. Cole–Cole α = 0.411–0.143 (1.8–2.3 K).",
